 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Illusive Mirage — Innate Technique (11th level)</em></p><p>At 11th level, you have decided that affecting the area around people can lead to strategic victory. As an action for 10 cursed energy, you can manipulate the surrounding terrain around you in a 150 ft radius in the following ways:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Rough Ground</strong>. You make the terrain appear difficult to traverse, when a creature attempts to walk in this area they must spend twice as much movement per 5 ft of travel.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Obstructing Illusion</strong>. As an action, you make a false structure or wall within range. A creature is convinced that the structure is real, meaning that they cannot target you with features that require line of sight.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A creature can attempt to see through the illusion by rolling an Investigation or Perception check (using their Cursed Energy score if they are a Sorcerer) against your Cursed Energy save DC. A creature automatically succeeds if they have an ability like true sight.  </p>",
